5(b).answer_md:
(i) Overheads Expenditure Variance

$$
\begin{aligned}
&= \text{Overheads Cost Variance (–) Overheads Volume Variance} \\
&= \text{₹ }2{,}800\text{(A)} - \text{₹ }2{,}000\text{(A)} \\
&= \text{₹ }800\text{(A)}
\end{aligned}
$$

(ii) Actual incurred overheads

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Overheads Expenditure Variance} &= \text{Budgeted Overheads (–) Actual Overheads} \\
\text{₹ }800\text{(A)} &= \text{₹ }12{,}000\text{ (–) Actual Overheads}
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, Actual Overheads $= \text{₹ }12{,}800$

(iii) Actual hours for actual production

$$
\begin{aligned}
&= \text{Actual Overhead} / \text{Actual Overhead Recovery Rate} \\
&= \text{₹ }12800/8 = 1{,}600\text{ Hrs.}
\end{aligned}
$$

(iv) Overheads Capacity Variance

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\text{Budgeted Overheads for Actual Hours (–) Budgeted Overheads} \\
&= \text{₹ }5 \times 1{,}600\text{ hrs.} - \text{₹ }12{,}000 \\
&= \text{₹ }8{,}000 - \text{₹ }12{,}000 \\
&= \text{₹ }4{,}000\text{ (A)}
\end{aligned}
$$

(v) Overheads efficiency variance

$$
\begin{aligned}
&= \text{Absorbed Overheads (–) Budgeted Overheads for Actual Hours} \\
&= \text{₹ }10{,}000 - \text{₹ }5 \times 1{,}600\text{ hours} \\
&= \text{₹ }2{,}000\text{ (F)}
\end{aligned}
$$

(vi) Standard hours for actual production

$$
\begin{aligned}
&= \text{Absorbed Overhead} / \text{Standard rate per hour} \\
&= \text{₹ }10{,}000/\text{₹ }5 \\
&= 2{,}000\text{ hrs}
\end{aligned}
$$

(vii) Calculation of Standard Rate/Hour

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Overhead Cost Variance} &= \text{Absorbed Overheads (–) Actual Overheads} \\
\text{₹ }2{,}800\text{ (A)} &= \text{Absorbed Overheads (–) ₹ }12{,}800 \\
\text{Absorbed Overheads} &= \text{₹ }10{,}000 \\
\text{Standard Rate per Hour} &= \text{Budgeted Overhead} / \text{Budgeted Hours} \\
&= \text{₹ }12{,}000/2{,}400\text{ hrs} \\
&= \text{₹ }5\text{ /hr}
\end{aligned}
$$
